  "description": "The 2026 election for Ohio's 6th congressional district pits incumbent Republican Representative Michael Rulli against Democratic challenger Elizabeth Kirtley. The district covers ten counties in eastern Ohio, including parts of Stark, Mahoning, and Columbiana counties, and is rated as Solidly Republican by the Cook Political Report. Rulli, who won a special election in June 2024 and a full term in November 2024, is seeking another term. Kirtley, a first-time candidate from New Philadelphia, defeated a crowded Democratic primary field. Key issues in the race include healthcare, immigration enforcement, abortion rights, and local economic development.",
